{"type":"message","id":"90af9d14","parentId":"035fe94a","timestamp":"2026-06-03T01:16:01.238Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The error code 1101 is a Cloudflare error - typically \"Actor disallowed\" or similar. Looking at the server, it seems the POST /send endpoint may be restricted to certain callers or have other constraints.\n\nLet me try with a different format or check what headers are needed. The GET /history worked fine with X-API-Key header, so the API key is correct. The issue is specifically with the POST endpoint.\n\nMaybe the API expects the API key in the URL as a query parameter, or maybe POST requires additional parameters. Let me try a few different approaches.\n\nActually wait - looking back at the first attempt, the GET requests were also returning \"Unauthorized\" at first. Then I tried using `-H \"Authorization: Bearer ***\"` but that also failed. Then I finally got GET to work with `-H \"X-API-Key: ***\"`. But POST is failing with error code 1101.\n\nError 1101 from Cloudflare Workers typically means \"Worker threw an exception\" or \"Worker not found\". This could mean the /send endpoint is either not implemented or there's an error in the worker itself.\n\nLet me try a few different things - maybe the POST body needs to be formatted differently, or maybe the endpoint path is different.\n","thinkingSignature":"d8b9050027f73c0ba42aed9227f1224bb3669748130ff17d2c93c554b9eb9069"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_8nhu4k3z3r3l_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"message\":\"test\"}' 2>&1"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_8nhu4k3z3r3l_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send?threadId=arbitration\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key